// ============================================================
// Catalog: the thinking around the event sources, the given contexts and the seed data - sticky notes on their canvases.
//
// A note says what a decision was, what is still open, what we assume and what could go wrong, beside the cards it is about.
// Colours: green decision, yellow question, blue assumption, pink risk. Authoring metadata only: it never reaches the running application.
// ============================================================

sticky note on eventsources
  description "[DECISION] Product is the one event source of the catalog. Every price, approval and withdrawal is an event on a product's own stream, so the history of one product reads top to bottom."
  colour green
  position 1210 150
  size 270 190

sticky note on eventsources
  description "[QUESTION] Should a product keep one stream per market (NO, SE, DK) once Sales prices per market? Today there is one Lifecycle stream and the market is a field."
  colour yellow
  position 1210 360
  size 270 190

sticky note on givencontexts
  description "[DECISION] One reusable context for 'a product that can be sold', so no specification repeats the drafting, pricing and approval events by hand."
  colour green
  position 1210 150
  size 270 190

sticky note on givencontexts
  description "[ASSUMPTION] A product is always priced before it is approved. A specification that needs an unpriced product states its own events instead of reusing this context."
  colour blue
  position 1210 360
  size 270 190

sticky note on seeddata
  description "[DECISION] The starter catalogue is the same eight products Storefront and Warehouse show in Preview, so a played application and the drawn screens agree."
  colour green
  position 560 150
  size 270 190

sticky note on seeddata
  description "[QUESTION] Do we seed approved products only, or also a draft and a withdrawn one to show the lifecycle?"
  colour yellow
  position 560 360
  size 270 190
